Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for React/Vite Project

## Overview
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this portfolio project following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (v1.4.1)
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Generated updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
- Modified `src/App.tsx` to import and use the Analytics component
- Added `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react"` at the top of the file
- Placed `<Analytics />` component inside the Router component, after the Layout wrapper
- This placement ensures analytics tracks all route changes throughout the application

### 3. Implementation Details
- Framework: React with Vite and TypeScript
- Integration method: React component import (`@vercel/analytics/react`)
- Component placement: Within the `<Router>` context to track navigation events
- No additional configuration required - Analytics component works out of the box

## Files Modified
- `frontend/src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

## Verification
✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing linting warnings/errors are pre-existing)
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ Bundle size impact: Analytics package adds minimal overhead

## Next Steps
To enable analytics in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Analytics data will begin appearing after users visit the deployed site

## Notes
- The Analytics component is designed to work seamlessly with Vercel deployments
- In development mode, analytics events are not sent to avoid polluting production data
- The component is lightweight and lazy-loads to minimize performance impact
